# Crew orchestrator error sentences.
error-crew-budget-exceeded = This crew has used up its allowance of AI calls.
error-crew-charter-invalid = The crew's brief isn't valid or its plan doesn't fit. Review the brief and try again.
error-crew-coordinator-unavailable = ordin couldn't be reached to coordinate the crew, even after a second try. Try again later.
error-crew-coordinator-unusable = ordin's answer to the crew couldn't be used. Try again.
error-crew-ended = This crew has already finished.
error-crew-end-reason-too-long = The reason for ending is too long. Keep it under 500 characters.
error-crew-guardrail-refused = A safety rule stopped the crew from handing that job on.
error-crew-limit-reached = The crew reached its limit for rounds, time or AI calls, so it stopped.
error-crew-member-failed-twice = A crew member failed twice on the same job, so the crew stopped.
error-crew-not-found = That crew wasn't found. It may have been removed.
error-crew-not-paused = That crew isn't paused, so it can't be continued.
error-crew-not-started-by-person = A crew only starts when you press the button to start it.
error-crew-pause-reason-mismatch = The crew's pause reason doesn't match whether it is paused. Refresh and try again.
error-crew-rounds-exceeded = The crew has gone past the number of rounds it was allowed.
error-crew-store-unavailable = ordin can't reach the crew's records right now. Try again in a moment.
error-crew-take-over-refused = ordin asked to take over the work, which isn't allowed here.
error-crew-too-many-members = A crew can have at most 8 members. Remove some and try again.
error-crew-workflow-mismatch = The crew's workflow needs both a name and a version, or neither.
error-round-decision-invalid = The coordinator's decision is empty or too long. Try again.
error-round-immutable = That round is closed and can't be changed.
error-round-number-gap = The crew's rounds aren't numbered in order from 1. Refresh and try again.
error-round-too-many-running = More crew members are running than the crew allows. Wait for one to finish.
error-step-call-cycle = A workflow can't call itself, directly or through others. Choose a different workflow to call.
error-step-call-invalid = A step can only call another workflow in the same workspace, up to 3 levels deep.
error-step-condition-invalid = The condition is empty or too long. Write it in 1 to 500 characters.
error-step-each-max-out-of-range = The most times a step can repeat for a list is between 1 and 50. Choose a number in that range.
error-step-each-not-list = A step can only repeat for a list. Choose a list input or an earlier step's list.
error-step-group-too-large = That group has more steps running together than your company allows. Make it smaller.
error-step-if-paths-out-of-range = A choice needs 2 to 4 paths, each with its own name of up to 40 characters.
error-step-line-invalid = A step's line must be one sentence of up to 200 characters.
error-step-nesting-too-deep = Steps are nested too deeply. Keep it to 4 levels.
error-step-position-invalid = A step's number isn't valid. Use digits and dots, with at most one letter at the end, in order.
error-step-too-many = A plan can have at most 50 steps and blocks in all. Remove some and try again.
error-step-until-max-out-of-range = The most times a step can repeat until done is between 1 and 10. Choose a number in that range.
error-step-uses-later-or-absent = A step can only use inputs and results from earlier steps on its own path.
